Description: face unlock for KDE Plasma
 Kenning signs you in with your face: on the lock screen, for sudo and, with
 its version of Plasma Login Manager, on the login screen. It works best with
 an infrared camera; an ordinary webcam can be used with a warning.
 .
 It includes a System Settings page to set it up, an animated face scan on
 the lock screen (Plasma 6.8 or newer) and installable animation themes.
 Recognition runs in a small service that owns the camera and the face models.
 .
 Fingerprints read by fprintd become a choice of their own on the lock screen
 and in administrator prompts, instead of a wait before the password.
